# BadmintonGPT environment variable template — copy to .env and fill in actual values
#   cp .env.example .env
# Both modes read this file:
#   (a) Docker Compose deployment (docs/DEPLOY.md) — docker compose substitutes ${VAR} directly.
#   (b) Local host mode (README.md) — scripts/load_env.sh loads it for ~/.nanobot/config.json resolution.
# Note: keys are read only from this project's .env, with no fallback to other projects.

# --- OpenAI (agent LLM, required) ---
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# Default agent model (nanobot/config.json uses ${NANOBOT_MODEL}). Bare name, without a provider prefix.
# If unset, both host mode (load_env.sh) and Docker (compose) fall back to gpt-5.5.
NANOBOT_MODEL=gpt-5.5

# --- Additional Custom model preset (optional; GPT-5.5 above remains the default) ---
# Wired in nanobot/config.json as providers.custom (OpenAI-compatible endpoint) + model_presets.custom.
# Adds a selectable "Custom (.env)" option to the WebUI Settings model menu. All three values are required;
# leave empty if unused. nanobot rejects unset ${VAR} values (but accepts empty strings), so load_env.sh/compose provide empty fallbacks.
# CUSTOM_MODEL_API_BASE=https://your-endpoint/v1   # openai SDK base_url (including /v1)
# CUSTOM_MODEL_API_KEY=sk-...
# CUSTOM_MODEL_API_MODEL=your-model-name           # Bare model name, without a provider prefix

# --- Message TTS (WebUI read-aloud button; optional) ---
# Gateway only; never included in the frontend bundle: the browser calls same-origin /api/tts, and the gateway proxies to TTS with the key.
# If unset, the read-aloud button returns 503 (feature disabled).
TTS_API_KEY=sk-...
# WebUI "Auto-prefetch speech" default: true = generate speech as soon as the reply finishes (instant playback); false (default) = generate only when the speaker button is clicked.
# Sent to the frontend via bootstrap as a default; each browser can override it in Settings → Speech.
TTS_AUTO_PREFETCH=false
# Optional overrides (all have defaults):
# TTS_API_BASE=https://llm.andyjjrt.cc/v1   # openai SDK base_url (automatically appends /audio/speech)
# TTS_API_MODEL=DGX/Qwen3-TTS
# TTS_DEFAULT_VOICE=chris  # Also the default in the WebUI voice dropdown
# Latency tuning (non-streaming proxy, synthesis takes ~0.1 s/character): the frontend splits each reply into TTS_SEGMENT_CHARS-character segments
# (sent to the browser via bootstrap); smaller segments produce sound sooner. Default 60 characters ≈ ~6 seconds to first sound. After editing, run `docker compose up -d`
# (no image rebuild needed). Constraint: TTS_SEGMENT_CHARS <= TTS_MAX_INPUT_CHARS (the server returns 413 if exceeded).
# TTS_SEGMENT_CHARS=60      # Characters per segment; ~0.1 s/character, so 60→~6s, 100→~10s
# TTS_MAX_INPUT_CHARS=300   # Server-side limit per segment (~0.1 s/character means a 60s timeout covers ~600 characters)
# TTS_TIMEOUT_S=60          # Gateway timeout in seconds for upstream TTS calls

# --- Cloudflare Access service tokens: one pair per remote MCP (approach A) ---
# badminton-reels (config.json uses ${REELS_CF_CLIENT_ID/SECRET})
REELS_CF_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.access
REELS_CF_CLIENT_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
# badminton-video-retrieval (config.json uses ${VIDEO_RETRIEVAL_CF_CLIENT_ID/SECRET})
VIDEO_RETRIEVAL_CF_CLIENT_ID=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx.access
VIDEO_RETRIEVAL_CF_CLIENT_SECRET=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# badminton-analyze (CoachAI; config.json uses ${ANALYZE_MCP_TOKEN})
# Exception: this server uses its own bearer token, not Cloudflare Access, so it does not follow the <NAME>_CF_CLIENT_ID/SECRET
# naming convention. Without it, the gateway fails at startup because ${VAR} is unset.
ANALYZE_MCP_TOKEN=xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# --- Docker Compose deployment (docs/DEPLOY.md; not needed in host mode) ---
# Connector token for a remotely managed Cloudflare tunnel (copy after creating it in Zero Trust → Networks → Tunnels).
# Configure ingress (badmintongpt.<zone> → http://gateway:8765) and the public hostname in the Cloudflare dashboard.
TUNNEL_TOKEN=eyJ...
# Public domain (documentation/verification reference only; actual ingress is configured in the dashboard)
BADMINTONGPT_HOSTNAME=badmintongpt.<your-zone>

# --- Required only for DB building (ingest profile), not at gateway runtime ---
# HuggingFace token (downloads shot-by-shot CSVs from the howard9199/Badminton dataset).
# ingest now includes its own parser (mcps/badminton-db/ingest_lib/) and no longer requires badminton-reels source.
HF_TOKEN=hf_...

# --- Optional (all have defaults; usually no need to set) ---
# Project root (defaults to the project path)
# BADMINTONGPT_HOME=/mnt/ssd1/howchien/badmintonGPT
# SQLite DB path (ingest.py / db MCP default = $BADMINTONGPT_HOME/data/badminton.db)
# BADMINTON_DB=/mnt/ssd1/howchien/badmintonGPT/data/badminton.db
# badminton-reels source/data paths for parity testing (mcps/badminton-db/scripts/test_decouple_parity.py; optional)
# REELS_SRC=/mnt/ssd1/howchien/badminton-reels/src
# REELS_DATA=/mnt/ssd1/howchien/badminton-reels/data/Data
